/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:13:AutoRE \citep{autore2024} fine-tunes LLMs with QLoRA using a relation-head-facts decomposition; \citet{xu2024lmrc} frame extraction as multi-choice reading comprehension; RelPrior \citep{wang2025relprior} uses relation priors to guide LLM-based extraction; GLiDRE \citep{zhang2025glidre} presents a generalist lightweight approach; Ru-LLM \citep{wang2025rullm} incorporates logical rule constraints; and \citet{chen2025docksrag} combine retrieval-augmented generation with structured knowledge.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-14-These methods match or surpass encoder baselines but produce bare triplets without evidence. Among LLM-based generative methods at the 8B scale, our RSFT model (54.33 Ign-F1 on DocRED dev) outperforms AutoRE (52.14\footnote{AutoRE Ign-F1 is from the LLaMA3-8B reproduction by \citet{wang2025relprior}; the original paper reports only F1.}) and is slightly below RelPrior ($-$1.17pp), while being the only method that additionally provides sentence-level evidence grounding.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-15-The critical distinction lies in computational nature: in SAIS and DREEAM, evidence retrieval is classification that regularizes the encoder without increasing output length; in LLM-based DocRE, evidence requires additional output tokens per triple, imposing costs that depend on model capacity and optimization strategy.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-16-Whether this cost is inevitable or can be mitigated is the central question of our work.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-17-
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-18-Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO; \citealt{shao2024deepseekmath}) eliminates the separate value network by computing advantages within groups.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-19-Subsequent work addresses failure modes: DAPO \citep{yu2025dapo} prevents entropy collapse, Dr.\ GRPO \citep{liu2025drgrpo} corrects length bias, and multi-objective variants \citep{liu2026gdpo,ito2025mogrpo} handle competing reward signals.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-20-Applications to structured IE include R1-RE \citep{dai2025r1re} and REAR \citep{wang2025rear}.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-21-Direct Preference Optimization \citep{rafailov2023direct} reformulates RLHF as implicit reward maximization.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-22-Our decoupling spectrum is distinct from catastrophic forgetting in RL alignment \citep{jin2025rl_panacea}, where models lose pre-trained capabilities across tasks; in our setting, extraction and evidence compete \emph{within} a single task, resembling negative transfer in multi-task learning \citep{ruder2017overview,standley2020tasks,yu2020gradient}, amplified by QLoRA's constrained parameter space \citep{gao2023scaling,moskovitz2024constrained}.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-23-RSFT avoids this intra-task competition by operating on discrete outputs rather than gradients, extending the sample-and-select principle \citep{wang2023selfconsistency} to structured IE with joint quality scoring.
--
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:28:\citet{zelikman2022star} introduced STaR for iterative self-improvement; \citet{dong2023raft} generalize this with reward-model-based sample filtering; recent analysis shows rejection sampling implicitly performs PPO-like optimization \citep{tang2025rsftppo}.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-29-Our RSFT is a single-round variant applied to evidence-grounded DocRE with CED/NLI scoring as a domain-specific quality filter.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/related_work.tex-30-Because RSFT selects complete outputs rather than differentiating through a reward signal, it cannot exploit the extraction-evidence trade-off that gradient methods discover, inherently preserving joint quality.
--
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:4:Recent LLM-based approaches have closed this gap: \citet{autore2024} fine-tune LLMs with structured decomposition, \citet{xu2024lmrc} frame it as multi-choice reading comprehension, and \citet{chen2025docksrag} combine retrieval-augmented generation with structured knowledge.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-5-These methods approach or surpass encoder baselines on DocRED \citep{yao2019docred} and Re-DocRED \citep{tan2022redocred} in extraction accuracy, yet every one outputs bare relation triplets $(e_h, r, e_t)$ without indicating \emph{which sentences} support each prediction.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-6-In deployment contexts---clinical knowledge bases, legal due-diligence pipelines, financial compliance systems---users cannot verify a prediction without manually locating its textual basis across a multi-page document.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-7-
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-8-Encoder-based methods have partially addressed this need: \citet{xiao2022sais} introduce sentence-level evidence supervision as an auxiliary signal, and \citet{ma2023dreeam} extend this with dynamic evidence retrieval through memory attention.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-9-Both produce evidence and improve extraction, but encoder methods now trail LLM-based approaches in accuracy.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-10-The community faces a gap: the most accurate extractors provide no evidence, while evidence-capable methods are no longer competitive.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-11-
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-12-This gap reflects a structural difference.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-13-In encoder methods, evidence retrieval is classification that regularizes the encoder at negligible cost; in LLM-based DocRE, evidence requires the model to \emph{generate} additional output tokens per triple, increasing output length and decoding complexity.
/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-14-The na\"{i}ve expectation is that this generation cost always harms extraction accuracy.
--
